WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
Some bacteria now resist
not one antibiotic,

2
00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:05.270
but several at once.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:11.540
In 1952, two scientists, the Lederbergs,
set out to test where resistance comes

4
00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:12.430
from.

5
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.350
They grew bacteria on a dish
with no antibiotic at all.

6
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.600
Then a velvet pad printed copies onto
dishes that did contain the drug.

7
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.560
Nobody designs a drug-resistant germ.

8
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:28.370
So how do whole populations
of them appear so quickly?

9
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.110
In this mission, you'll read
the Lederbergs' results,

10
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.660
position by position, dish by dish.

11
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.360
Then you'll find out why resistance can
sweep through a population in just a few

12
00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.600
days.

13
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:45.390
Your mission: explain how resistant
populations appear so quickly,

14
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.990
when nobody designs them.
